Java Practice Five,Custom Annotation,"Define a custom annotation `@MyTest` that can be applied to methods."
Java Practice Five,Decorator Design Pattern,"Implement the Decorator pattern to add new functionality (e.g. milk, sugar) to a base `Coffee` object at runtime."
Java Practice Five,Foreign Function & Memory API (Conceptual),"In a comment, explain the purpose of the Foreign Function & Memory API (Project Panama)."
Java Practice Five,HTTP Client (GET Request),"Use `java.net.http.HttpClient` (Java 11+) to send a synchronous GET request to a public API and print the response body."
Java Practice Five,HTTP Client (POST Request),"Use the `HttpClient` to send a POST request with a JSON body to an endpoint."
Java Practice Five,JDBC - Database Connection,"Write the code to establish a basic JDBC connection to a database (e.g. H2, SQLite)."
Java Practice Five,JDBC - Reading a `ResultSet`,"Iterate through a `ResultSet` from a query and print the values from each row."
Java Practice Five,JDBC - Transaction Management,"Demonstrate transaction management by using `setAutoCommit(false)`, `commit()`, and `rollback()`."
Java Practice Five,JDBC - `INSERT` Statement,"Use a `PreparedStatement` to insert a new row of data into a database table."
Java Practice Five,JDBC - `PreparedStatement` Query,"Use a `PreparedStatement` to execute a `SELECT` query on a database table with a `WHERE` clause."
