Java Practice Five,Method Handles,"Use a `MethodHandle` to dynamically find and invoke a method on an object."
Java Practice Five,Micro-benchmarking with JMH (Conceptual),"Write a comment explaining what the Java Microbenchmark Harness (JMH) is and what a basic benchmark method looks like."
Java Practice Five,NIO.2 - Memory-Mapped Files,"Use a `MappedByteBuffer` to read a large file, demonstrating memory-mapped I/O."
Java Practice Five,NIO.2 - Walking a File Tree,"Use `Files.walkFileTree()` to recursively visit all files and directories starting from a given path."
Java Practice Five,NIO.2 - Watching a Directory,"Use the `WatchService` API to monitor a directory for file creation, modification, and deletion events."
Java Practice Five,Observer Design Pattern,"Implement the Observer design pattern where a `Subject` object maintains a list of `Observer` objects and notifies them of state changes."
Java Practice Five,Parallel Stream,"Convert a stream operation to a `parallelStream()` and measure the performance difference on a large dataset."
Java Practice Five,Phantom References,"Create a `PhantomReference` and a `ReferenceQueue`. Explain in a comment how they are used for pre-mortem cleanup actions."
Java Practice Five,Processing Annotations with Reflection,"Write a program that uses reflection to find all methods in a class that are marked with your `@MyTest` annotation and invoke them."
Java Practice Five,Record Serialization,"Create a `record` that implements `Serializable` and demonstrate that it can be written to and read from an `ObjectOutputStream`."
Java Practice Five,Reflection - Modifying `private` Fields,"Use reflection to access and modify the value of a `private` field in an object."
Java Practice Five,Sealed Interfaces,"Create a `sealed` interface that `permits` only a specific set of classes to implement it."
Java Practice Five,Strategy Design Pattern,"Implement the Strategy pattern to define a family of algorithms (e.g. different sorting strategies) and make them interchangeable."
Java Practice Five,Stream `mapMulti()`,"Use `mapMulti()` (Java 16+) as an alternative to `flatMap` for a one-to-many transformation of stream elements."
Java Practice Five,Switch Expressions,"Use a `switch` expression (Java 14+) to return a value, simplifying a traditional `switch` statement."
Java Practice Five,The `StackWalker` API,"Use the `StackWalker` API (Java 9+) to efficiently traverse the current thread's call stack and get information about it."
Java Practice Five,Virtual Threads (Conceptual),"Write a comment explaining the concept of Virtual Threads (Project Loom) and their benefits."
Java Practice Five,Weak References,"Create a `WeakReference` to an object. Suggest garbage collection and show that the reference becomes null."
Java Practice Five,`AtomicInteger`,"Use `AtomicInteger` to safely increment a counter from multiple threads without using `synchronized` blocks."
Java Practice Five,`Callable` and `Future`,"Submit a `Callable` to an `ExecutorService` that returns a string after a short delay. Use the `Future` object to retrieve and print the result."
Java Practice Five,`CompletableFuture` (Asynchronous Computation),"Create a `CompletableFuture` that runs a task asynchronously to supply a result."
Java Practice Five,`CountDownLatch`,"Use a `CountDownLatch` to make a main thread wait until three worker threads have completed their tasks."
Java Practice Five,`ExecutorService` for Task Submission,"Create an `ExecutorService` with a fixed thread pool and submit a simple `Runnable` task to it."
Java Practice Five,`HttpClient` (Asynchronous Request),"Send an asynchronous GET request using the `HttpClient` and use a `CompletableFuture` to process the response."
Java Practice Five,`InputStream.transferTo()`,"Use `transferTo()` (Java 9+) to efficiently copy data from an `InputStream` to an `OutputStream`."
Java Practice Five,`Optional.stream()`,"Use `Optional.stream()` (Java 9+) to convert an `Optional` into a stream of either zero or one element."
Java Practice Five,`ReentrantLock`,"Use a `ReentrantLock` to protect a critical section of code in a multithreaded context as an alternative to `synchronized`."
Java Practice Five,`Semaphore`,"Use a `Semaphore` to limit the number of threads that can access a specific resource concurrently."
Java Practice Five,`StampedLock`,"Use a `StampedLock` to perform an optimistic read, and show how it can be upgraded to a pessimistic read lock if needed."
