Language Elements,Book Information,"Declare variables to store information about a book: title (String), author (String), publication year (int), and price (double). Use meaningful identifiers."
Language Elements,Boolean Logic,"Declare boolean variables and initialize them with boolean literals. Perform logical operations and print the results."
Language Elements,Character Literals,"Declare character variables and initialize them with different character literals, including Unicode escape sequences."
Language Elements,Circle Calculations,"Create a program to calculate the circumference and area of a circle. Use identifiers for the radius and pi, and a literal for the value of pi."
Language Elements,Comment Types,"Write a program that includes single-line, multi-line, and documentation comments to explain different parts of the code."
Language Elements,Escape Sequence Practice,"Write a program that uses various escape sequences in a string literal to format the output (e.g. newline, tab, backslash)."
Language Elements,Final Keyword Example,"Declare a constant using the 'final' keyword and attempt to reassign it to demonstrate that it's a compile-time error. Use comments to explain."
Language Elements,Identifier Naming Conventions,"Create a program with variables that demonstrate both good and bad identifier naming conventions. Use comments to explain why certain names are good or bad."
Language Elements,Keyword Identifier,"Write a program that declares variables using at least five different Java keywords. Add comments to explain the purpose of each variable."
Language Elements,Literal Showcase,"Declare variables of different data types and initialize them with various literals (integer, floating-point, character, string, boolean)."
Language Elements,Null Literal,"Declare an object reference variable and initialize it to the null literal. Add a comment explaining what a null reference means."
Language Elements,Student Grades,"Create a program that stores a student's name and their grades in three subjects. Use appropriate identifiers and literals."
Lifecycle,"InstanceVariableLifecycle","Explain that an instance variable's lifecycle is tied to the object it belongs to."
Lifecycle,"LocalVariableLifecycle","In a method, print a variable's value. Explain that the variable only exists while the method is executing."
